title A witness nobody runs guards nothing -- 1,690 on disk, 56 sung every lap, and a ceiling that had been crossed for two laps
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Opened cold: sh tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_run.sh read guards_run=58 guards_green=58 run_verdict=ok on the untouched tree, and every living row in construction/REDS.md read CLOSED. No standfast in force, so constructive work could open.
think Lap index from git log --oneline | wc -l = 3428, so the council rota reads row 3428 mod 5 = 3 -- Water and Venus, care and flow: the shape you grew and the shape you are, the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. The Gall/Conway row governed this lap exactly. Its own reading of this tree is an organization of one durable person and forgetful agents whose only channel is written artifacts, and a witness is the form a claim takes to travel between sessions. This lap asked how many of those claims anything actually reads.
think The two newest recommends converged on one crux and named it the same way: caravan_suite_witness stands off the standing roster, the already-named class of 1,683 witnesses on disk where 56 are gated. active-designing/20260824-080208 had booked the question in words -- whether every witness on disk is reached by something, which means tracing reachability rather than comparing counts -- and left it open as a round of its own. Took that round.
think Wrote tools/fixtures/witness_reach_scan.sh: it globs git ls-files for every tracked *_witness.rish, walks every tracked .rish and .sh for paths in INVOCATION position, and prints four readings -- total, standing (transitive closure from the roster), sung (named by any runner), unheard (named by nothing). Discovery rather than a list, and the roots are read off construction/standing-equipment.kyri so the meter stays true when the roster changes.
think The call/mention line is the whole difficulty and it took four prototypes. A loose rule that counted any path in a non-comment line read 452 reached; it was counting a grep argument in crypto_count_guard_witness.rish:73 as a call, which would have reported the entire 74-file crypto family as covered by the standing roster. A too-tight rule that skipped .rish after the bracket forms read 252; it was missing run ["sh" "-c" "rishi/bin/rishi run x"], which the buhr family genuinely uses. The rule that holds is command position applied uniformly, with a -c payload unwrapped and read the same way.
think My own bug, and it is worth writing down. The awk hung on almost every file once commands() was called inside the -c while loop. Cause: commands() runs match() of its own, and match() sets the GLOBAL RSTART and RLENGTH. When its inner match failed, RLENGTH became -1, so the outer loop's line = substr(line, RSTART + RLENGTH) returned the whole line and never advanced. Saving st and ln immediately after the outer match fixed it. A helper that reads a global is a helper that writes it.
think Then the meter's first real act. caravan_suite_witness had never been run in this arc, so I ran it: RED at caravan_ladder_carry_witness, carried=58550 against a ceiling of 58532 that only falls. Walked it back commit by commit with git archive into a pen -- 2a9ccea972 read 58532 exactly, 053dba9e5f read 58541, c10334408c read 58550. Two laps had shipped past a ceiling and both had recorded a green cold roster, honestly, because the roster never runs that meter.
think Booked REDS %219 and closed it root-first rather than by raising anything. The cause was one body: a nine-line entry point standing byte for byte in ten study rungs, growing by one copy on each lap that added a rung. Lifted it into caravan/study_door.rye as pub fn answer(comptime rung: type, init) taking the rung as a comptime type parameter -- the same shape ladder_checks.rye already uses for the supervision cohort -- and each of the ten now calls a three-line stub. Its own module rather than a row in ladder_checks.rye, because that harness imports twenty rungs and a study probe should stay standalone.
think The fold reached further than the ten modules, which is the honest cost of the shape. Nine pen controls build a study module from a copied source, so each needed caravan/study_door.rye copied in beside it. Three of them (objects, refusals, reply) build a mutated copy in $build_dir and had to be patched a second way. All ten study witnesses GREEN afterward, and each program's behavior is identical: table prints, selftest passes, an unknown argument still exits 1.
think Four more spelled numbers came out of the same root, and naming them together is the point. caravan_ladder_carry_witness spells carried=X ceiling=X so the ceiling sits exactly on the measurement with no slack; caravan_ladder_print_witness and caravan_ladder_spine_witness each spell a module denominator; caravan_ladder_reach_visibility_witness spells a three-number sink total. Every one of them had been stale since allowances.rye and address_space.rye landed, and every one was unheard for the same reason.
obs The measurement when the meter first read the tree: 1,690 tracked witnesses, 56 sung every lap by the roster, 512 named in an invocation position by any runner on disk, 1,178 named by nothing at all. The biggest unheard families are ales 239, equinox 123, hunk 86, mycelium 69, glow 61, font5x7 45. One roster row then moved standing from 56 to 167, since seating caravan_suite_witness carries its 111 rungs with it -- the staged tree reads 167 / 513 / 1,177 and the ceiling sits on 1,177 with no slack.
obs Rostered caravan_suite_witness on measured cost rather than on principle, and had to correct the measurement before it shipped. The first timing read 2m41s and I nearly wrote it onto the card; that run had ABORTED EARLY on the carry red this lap went on to close, so it sang a fraction of the roster and stopped. A failing run is faster than a passing one by construction. Re-timed on an idle pier after the fix: 8m31s for 111 rungs, 4.6 seconds a witness. crypto_suite_witness reads GREEN at 9m06s for 74, which is 7.4 seconds a witness because each rung rebuilds a crypto source.
obs The ceiling is a ratchet at 1,177 with no slack, rather than a wall at zero. A wall at zero would refuse every ordinary lap and a wall that refuses ordinary work is a wall somebody turns off. A witness born today is born sung, which is the same discipline exec-bit.md keeps for the mode bit.
obs Proved the guard from both sides on planted git repositories -- eighteen behaviors, eight call shapes heard, five mention shapes refused, and the ceiling read from three positions: one past it refuses, exactly at it passes, and removing a plant carries a refusing reading back to green. The control caught its own bug on the way: git add -A after removing a plant re-added the untracked file the previous reading had just proven invisible, so the count never moved. It uses git rm now.
obs The honest limit is written into the scan's own header. tools/hooks/pre-commit invokes through a variable, so unheard is an UPPER bound on what is truly unrun rather than an exact count, and the falsifier is stated: find a witness this meter calls unheard that some standing process actually runs. Five unheard names were traced by hand out of 1,177 -- ad_walk_sample, dated_classify, place_paint, crypto_suite, equinox_copy_sameness_almanac -- and each is genuinely named by no runner. The roster's own total wall time went untimed this lap and is left unclaimed rather than estimated.
obs Graded every artifact. The design note read B+ at 89 with a 44% negative-sentence share against Field's 30%, so it took a Gauge sweep; after the sweep and the corrections below it reads A at 96 with 16%. The scan, the control, the witness and study_door.rye each read A+ at 100. Nothing below B, so no molt frame was pushed.
