file construction/standing-equipment.kyri two rows -- witness_reach, and caravan_suite at a measured 8m31s
file construction/REDS.md %219 booked and closed; %218 folded to keep the pin under its bound
file active-designing/20260825-092953_what-a-roster-owes-a-run.md the argument, the costs, and what stays proposed
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now refilled, the guard count and the landed row moved
obs Stopped and restarted the hot roster twice rather than letting it measure a tree the commit would not ship. Both times a read-through found a stale number in prose the run had already walked past -- a cost paragraph still quoting the corrected timing, and a falsifier claiming ten hand-traced names where five were traced. REDS %174 asks that the hot green measure the tree the commit ships, and a run that overlaps an edit measures neither tree. Cheaper to restart at guard one than to publish a green that means something else.
recommend keep-going the second roster tier is the next crux and the cost measurement makes it urgent rather than tidy -- the Caravan choir adds a measured 8m31s to every roster run and the roster is read twice a lap, so a tier field in construction/standing-equipment.kyri is what decides whether the next choir can be heard at all; beside it a choir for ales would lift 239 of the 1,177 unheard in one round
